": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "An Emotional Week", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Emotional Intelligence", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to talk about things that were possible in the past and may or may not have happened. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The structure: <br/><br/> Subject    + modal verb    + have     + verb (past participle)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I             could              have        done<br/> You             should              have        made<br/> She            would               have        said</span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> to talk about possibilities if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">Having this information last week could have helped me.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to talk about past events that did not happen and to speculate about events that may or may not have happened.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I should have read about it before now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to speculate negatively about what may or may not have happened.<br/> You also use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to express regret for past actions.<br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to imagine a result if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\"> I probably would have coped better with stress at work if I had been more familiar with EI.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "* <span class=\"italic\">Would have</span> expresses more certainty about the outcome or result than <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I should have read about it before now because it is very interesting to me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Having this information last week could have helped me with my interactions with my boss.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I probably would have coped better with stress at work if I had been more familiar with EI.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I should have done this research a long time ago! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you need to change the verb to a tense further back in time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had</span> already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">eaten</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"Where do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">live</span>?\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You have to change the pronoun if you want to report what someone else said. Compare the two sentences below. In both cases the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\">I</span> didn't want to go.</li> <li>Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\">he</span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense.<br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">can</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I asked myself what I could do about it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " A friend told me I had to learn more about managing my emotions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A co-worker told me I needed to learn to communicate clearly and manage conflict.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "People at work said that I could be more productive if I could communicate better.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to recognize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be able to identify someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Emotional Intelligence (EI) is how we describe our ability to recognize both our own emotions and the emotions of others. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to differentiate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tell the difference between things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is difficult to  differentiate between different feelings. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "potent ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very effective or strong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Those people who have a high EI are generally in better mental health, show stronger job performance, and are more potent in their leadership skills.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to boost", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to increase the force, power, or amount of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Apparently it's possible to boost your EI level.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to navigate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to control the direction of ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It does this by helping you navigate through the workplace and its social complexities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "complexity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the quality of being complicated or hard to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a lot of social complexity in businesses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to excel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be very good at something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It will help you to excel in your career.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On the Internet, research Emotional Intelligence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make detailed notes on the information you find.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use your notes to create a presentation about Emotional Intelligence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your information to your class or to a group.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about reactions and behavior in a work situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use reported speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I react to things going wrong and talk about hypothetical situations about the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present information to a group.", "type": "text"}]}]}